576 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/T (There are limits to the breaking down of production into many small tasks. Perhaps the greatest is that the division of labour may eventually reduce efficiency and increase unit costs, because repetitive work lowers worker motivation and productivity. Workers begin to take less pride in their work and quality suffers. Some of these laborious tasks have been automated and, with the advent of robotics, this negative aspect may be less significant nowadays. The division of labour also runs the risk that if one machine breaks down \(or an individual is absent\) then the entire production process stops. Some workers receive narrow training and may not be able to find alternative jobs if they find themselves out of work \(they may suffer structural unemployment\). Another disadvantage is that mass-produced standardised goods tend to lack variety.)
/E (There are limits to the breaking down of production into many small tasks. Perhaps the greatest is that the division of labour may eventually reduce efficiency and increase unit costs, because repetitive work lowers worker motivation and productivity. Workers begin to take less pride in their work and quality suffers. Some of these laborious tasks have been automated and, with the advent of robotics, this negative aspect may be less significant nowadays. The division of labour also runs the risk that if one machine breaks down \(or an individual is absent\) then the entire production process stops. Some workers receive narrow training and may not be able to find alternative jobs if they find themselves out of work \(they may suffer structural unemployment\). Another disadvantage is that mass-produced standardised goods tend to lack variety.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
